body:
Closes #239 after merge.

Fixes invalid ARIA list-item semantics inside the CV assistant transcript while preserving the existing `role="log"` live-region model recommended for chat history.

Scope:
- remove `role="listitem"` from the initial chat greeting;
- stop assigning `role="listitem"` to dynamically appended chat messages;
- preserve `role="log"`, `aria-live="polite"`, `aria-relevant="additions"`, `aria-atomic="false"`, streaming, history, focus handling and status announcements;
- add focused regression coverage;
- rebuild deterministic frontend dist from authoritative source.

The final branch is one clean commit directly on current main. The branch-only build helper used to produce the deterministic Vite output has been fully removed and is not present in the final tree or PR diff.

No backend, CVBot, nginx, Cloudflare, DB, secret, host, deployment-control or production mutation. Expected deployment classification after merge: `AUTO_DEPLOY_SAFE`.

## Intent

Fix issues #149 and #153 together so a second live account grant opens an area the signed-in product actually leads to. Captain decision 2026-08-13: add an area switcher to the shared signed-in header for accounts with more than one granted area, while single-area accounts keep the existing header chrome; make sign-in honor the same-origin returnTo page the person came from when it is inside any area opened by the full live grant union, including a narrower grant, while retaining the existing predictable home when there is no valid return path. On pages outside every granted area, the switcher must use a disabled placeholder option labeled Go to... as its controlled value, never display the first granted area as current, and selecting any granted area including the first must fire a real change and navigate. Tests must prove a multi-grant account can reach every granted area from the header everywhere, the sign-in return journey, the public-page placeholder behavior, and unchanged single-grant behavior in real desktop and mobile browsers. Stay within the shared signed-in header and auth landing redirect fence. Keep the area model data-driven from the account grant union so the later sb-attendee-accounts work can add an attendee area without hard-coding the three current areas. The PR body must include Closes #149 and Closes #153.

## What Changed

- `GET /api/session` now returns the full live grant union as `roles` beside the describing `role`, and `client/lib.tsx` derives areas from that union (`roleAreas`, `switchableAreasFor`, `accountAreasFor`). A new `AreaSwitcher` renders in the shared signed-in header and on the submitter dashboard for accounts holding more than one granted area; single-area accounts keep the existing chrome, and the extra portal/proposal fetches now run only for the single-grant speaker shape they affect.
- On a page outside every granted area the switcher's controlled value is a disabled `Go to...` placeholder rather than the first area, so no option claims a location the person is not at and selecting any area — including the first — fires a change and navigates.
- `signedInDestination` resolves `?returnTo` and honours it when it resolves same-origin into `/submitter` or any area the grant union opens, falling back to the account's landing area when the reference will not parse, leaves the origin, only shares a prefix with an area root, or lands outside every grant; `client/App.tsx` routes sign-in through it.
- Adds unit coverage for area derivation and return-path resolution, an integration assertion on the session payload's roles, and a browser test that a two-grant account reaches both granted areas from the header; plus switcher styles in `client/styles.css` and `submitter.css` and AGENTS.md/README notes.

Closes #149
Closes #153

## Risk Assessment

✅ Low: The change is well-bounded client chrome plus one additive session field; the returnTo guard now resolves-then-judges and rejects every hostile and malformed input I traced, single-grant and attendee chrome is provably unchanged, and the only two findings are non-functional (an unreachable branch and already-compensated CSS scoping).

## Testing

Ran the focused unit (16), Workers-integration (13), and end-to-end account-access suites — the latter on both the desktop Chromium and mobile iPhone 13/WebKit Playwright projects, all passing — then proved the change is what fixes the reported behavior by reverting client/ and worker/ to the base commit, watching the two-grant header test fail because no "Switch area" control exists, and restoring the target source to see it pass again. For product-level evidence I drove a live local Worker in both browsers: a freshly signed-up account was granted a second area by the seeded organizer, and screenshots show the header switcher listing exactly the two granted areas on /reviewer and /speaker, the disabled "Go to..." placeholder as the value on the public /program page and the submitter dashboard with the first granted area still navigating when chosen, the sign-in return journey landing back on /speaker from /login?returnTo=%2Fspeaker, and a single-grant account keeping its unchanged "My schedule" header link with no switcher. Only a cosmetic label-clipping observation in the open mobile nav; the worktree was left clean with transient .wrangler and test-results removed.

